in. </p><p>In case you lose your device or uninstall the application, you will need one of the following backup codes to access to your account: </p><ul><li>bebe6fa06e9c</li><li>9a8181fff748</li><li>4ed85ff5521f</li><li>0f52deec5cfa</li><li>5308dfb3eeba</li><li>a5d15d7b03fe</li><li>95e28ed9d0a3</li><li>bdf0c9fbd083</li><li>c0a9c26a46e0</li><li>db3d08f886eb</li></ul><br><p>Make sure to write these down (preferably on paper) and store them in a safe location, otherwise you may  <strong>permanently lose access</strong> to your account. </p></div><p>Two factor authentication is currently <strong>enabled</strong> for your account. </p><h4>Enter the generated 6-digit code or one of your backup codes to disable.</h4><p>Note that the 6-digit codes are limited to a single use within their lifespan of 30 seconds, so if you just logged in with a code, entering it again here will cause an error. If that's the case, just wait for a new code to be generated. </p><div class="field"><input class="input" id="user_twofactor_token" name="user[twofactor_token]" placeholder="6-digit code" type="text"></div><br><div class="block block--fixed block--warning"><div class="field"><input class="input" id="user_current_password" name="user[current_password]" placeholder="Current password" type="password"></div><div class="fieldlabel">We need your current password to confirm these changes </div><br><button class="button" type="submit">Save Account</button></div></form><p><a href="/registrations/edit">Back</a></p></main><footer id="footer"><div id="footer_content"><div class="footercol"><h5 class="hide-mobile">Site Resources</h5><h2 class="hide-desktop">Site Resources</h2><strong><a href="/rules" target="_self">Site Rules</a></strong><br><strong><a href="/pages/privacy" target="_self">Privacy Policy</a></strong><br><strong><a href="/pages/tags" target="_self">Tag Guidelines</a></strong><br><a href="/pages/uploading" target="_self">About Uploading</a><br><a href="/pages/spoilers" target="_self">S